From: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:34:04 -0700
Subject: Protect against illegal layer modification during WillCommit

Original change's description:
> [HiC] Protect against illegal layer modification during WillCommit
>
> This guards against a call path wherein JS code running in a paint event
> handler can synchronously try to remove a cc::Layer from the layer tree
> (which is forbidden). With this change, LayerTreeHost maintains a list
> of layers that that should be removed as soon as the commit is finished.
>
> Fixed: 576097084,510426944
> Change-Id: I42e444e977cc9178d169169b766e9aab271a00e8
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8641078
> Reviewed-by: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1727394}

(cherry picked from commit 63d3b40075f34bcac9fe09b23aa63e1379d34ba1)

Bug: 578326081,576097084,510426944
Change-Id: I42e444e977cc9178d169169b766e9aab271a00e8

